{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1207483-lets-discuss-making-a-gargoyle-kith","id":1207483,"title":"Lets discuss making a Gargoyle Kith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-15T19:25:52-07:00","id":1207483,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Lets discuss making a Gargoyle Kith","content":"So one of the ideas I had, and I remember a few others brought up, was creating a Kith similar to the Gargoyles from the old disney cartoon. So the idea would be Fae, lets say some Inanimae so the Dreams/Myths of the very Elements chose to take refuge in the Flesh. So they are like a mix of the Inanimae, in their primal inhuman dreams, and the Merfolk, who took refuge in the flesh but breed within their own communities living away from humanity.<br /> <br /> So the Gargoyles are born from Eggs that come from Gargoyle pairs, or human/Gargoyle pairings. They are raised in private groups, and to help shield from Banality they turn to stone the moment the Sun Rises and return to flesh by night.<br /> <br /> They would say perhaps have Houses for different types of statues, or possibly different Kiths.<br /> <br /> House F<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u00f3sh\u012b</span></span></span>: For Fu Lions and Fu Dogs, and Sacred Guardian Beasts like Dragons and Directional Beasts. Homeland originated in East Asia.<br /> <br /> House Shedu: For Guardians of Necropoli, and plumbers of Underworld lore. They Originated in Egypt, but also include the Sumerian Bearded Lion/Bull iconography.<br /> <br /> House Babewyn: The standard Gargoyles, Grotesques and Chimera statues popularly found in Cathedrals, originated in France and spread the quickest and farthest of all the Houses. Guardians of the cities and highest points.<br /> <br /> House <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u015aakra: Those gargoyles invoking demonic guardians like Asura, and Animal headed and horned guardians of hell, originating in Buddhist Territories ranging from Indian, Tibet, and Japan.<br /> <br /> House Binesi: Gargoyles invoking the Totempole Iconography, these Gargoyles actually turn into Wood during the day and take the form of Clan Totem animals and even the Thunderbird. They are a house of Teachers.<br /> <br /> House Kisin: Statues of Death and Skeletons originating in the Americas, the represent Gods such as Mictlantecuhtli and skeletal motiffs. They embrace cannibalism, death and rebirth.<br /> <br /> Maybe though they call their Houses Clans, invoking the Doodem of the Ojibwe.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> So maybe include Birthrights for Flying, and a physical Boost. Maybe for nonhumanoid shapes they can switch between humanoid and beast form.<br /> <br /> What are some thoughts and ideas for these Gallain? I'm thinking they heal all bashing Damage and one Lethal while in stone slumber. Maybe they also convert one agg to Lethal too.<br /> <br /> They would also have Fae beasts, similar to how Gargoyles had Bronx and Boudicca?<br /> <br /> I think this would be most fun in the Changeling setting rather then their own thing, but they would likely touch upon Wraith and the Fera as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T20:14:14-07:00","id":1207507,"title":"","content":"It seems an odd choice to base them SO heavily on Disney's Gargoyles when they are very much not children of Oberon in said material. If there's a more objectively &quot;prodigal&quot; type its them.<br /> <br /> Might I suggest pushing it to that level, one creature type that objectively proves the Prodigal story...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T20:33:51-07:00","id":1207518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1207483-lets-discuss-making-a-gargoyle-kith?p=1207507#post1207507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems an odd choice to base them SO heavily on Disney's Gargoyles when they are very much not children of Oberon in said material. If there's a more objectively &quot;prodigal&quot; type its them.<br /> <br /> Might I suggest pushing it to that level, one creature type that objectively proves the Prodigal story...</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but that is why I see them as Gallain. The Children of Oberon would then be the Kithain, but exclude things like the Inanimae.<br /> <br /> But the Show also didn't give them magic, outside of Demona.<br /> <br /> But I'd be interested in opinions on making them Prodigals. So they wouldn't use Arts, would be immune to Banality but I would still have to invent powers for them which they very much didn't have in the show. They would what naturally be attuned to the Dreaming?<br /> <br /> I mean Gallain seem to fit the Prodigal story more then the Prodigals...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T21:26:54-07:00","id":1207531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1207483-lets-discuss-making-a-gargoyle-kith?p=1207518#post1207518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but that is why I see them as Gallain. The Children of Oberon would then be the Kithain, but exclude things like the Inanimae.<br /> <br /> But the Show also didn't give them magic, outside of Demona.</div> </div> </div> </div>And all the Children of Oberon HAD magic. They also did have the old Gods as children of Oberon<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I'd be interested in opinions on making them Prodigals. So they wouldn't use Arts, would be immune to Banality but I would still have to invent powers for them which they very much didn't have in the show. They would what naturally be attuned to the Dreaming?<br /> <br /> I mean Gallain seem to fit the Prodigal story more then the Prodigals... </div> </div> </div>Make them a natural Kinain lineage. Related but not children of oberon.. then it explains why they have such lesser access to magics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T21:35:32-07:00","id":1207535,"title":"","content":"Yeah but if they are going to be player characters already assumed to be equals to changelings if you make them Kinain then they have some Magic, which already diverges from the show, and they would also have some other powers, likely physical.<br /> <br /> And I know the Old Gods where Children of Oberon. What I am saying is in this setting they recognize the Kithain as Children of Oberon but not themselves, and not the Inanimae. Saying that maybe they only consider the Dreams of Man to be the Children of Oberon.<br /> <br /> But if they were some sort of naturally Kinain like species that would be interesting. Then they could actually be their own splat with their chosen Clan and probably one other type of Supernatural Axis. Maybe being a bit more like Werefolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T20:45:07-07:00","id":1208698,"title":"","content":"Hmm though did realize this puts Gargoyles within the last thousand years rather then them being an ancient species of fae. But maybe touches upon older stuff with their evocation of old iconography.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T21:40:04-07:00","id":1208717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1207483-lets-discuss-making-a-gargoyle-kith?p=1207518#post1207518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but that is why I see them as Gallain. The Children of Oberon would then be the Kithain, but exclude things like the Inanimae.<br /> <br /> But the Show also didn't give them magic, outside of Demona.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sadly, the Disney's version of them being guardians and placing their duty above personal gain or satisfaction has already been covered by the Trolls. So designing them around that would be kind of redundant. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> But luckily for us, not all &quot;changelings&quot; have to be members of the Fae specifically.<br /> <br /> Take the Hsein for example, who openly claim to have a completely different origin story, purpose and even a way of life compared to their western neighbors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-19-2018, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T02:36:19-07:00","id":1208777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1207483-lets-discuss-making-a-gargoyle-kith?p=1208698#post1208698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm though did realize this puts Gargoyles within the last thousand years rather then them being an ancient species of fae. But maybe touches upon older stuff with their evocation of old iconography.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven\u2019t read the whole thread, but I wanted to chime in on this. The wolpertinger in C20 are a young kith. They\u2019ve only been Kithain for roughly 50 years.<br /> <br /> 1000 years ago would be before the Shattering, when new fae races being born was a bit more common. There\u2019s plenty of room in the game for a youngish kith. Don\u2019t let that stop you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:38:47-07:00","id":1209453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1207483-lets-discuss-making-a-gargoyle-kith?p=1208777#post1208777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haven\u2019t read the whole thread, but I wanted to chime in on this. The wolpertinger in C20 are a young kith. They\u2019ve only been Kithain for roughly 50 years.<br /> <br /> 1000 years ago would be before the Shattering, when new fae races being born was a bit more common. There\u2019s plenty of room in the game for a youngish kith. Don\u2019t let that stop you.</div> </div> </div> </div>PK,do you think a powerful enough changeling sorcerer,or a group of them, could replicate the process of turning chimera into kithain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T22:16:01-07:00","id":1209512,"title":"","content":"A group could do most anything with enough glamour and numbers. It would be a significant and momentous event though, probably taking advantage of a singular miracle, like the turning of the Millenium or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T22:41:33-07:00","id":1209520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1207483-lets-discuss-making-a-gargoyle-kith?p=1209453#post1209453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PK,do you think a powerful enough changeling sorcerer,or a group of them, could replicate the process of turning chimera into kithain?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think about Mage-type-Sorcerer, who are also Changelings, thank to the writers, there is no such a thing.<br /> <br /> But with enough Naming and Arts, powermongering Merits and a good Bunk almost anything is possible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T22:43:18-07:00","id":1209522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1207483-lets-discuss-making-a-gargoyle-kith?p=1209520#post1209520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you think about Mage-type-Sorcerer, who are also Changelings, thank to the writers, there is no such a thing.<br /> <br /> But with enough Naming and Arts, powermongering Merits and a good Bunk almost anything is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope,I meant &quot;sorcerer&quot; as in a changeling who knows a lot of Arts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T07:02:16-07:00","id":1209608,"title":"","content":"I didnt watch a lot of the show, so I'm thinking more in the terms of making a Gargoyle Kith than a Kith of the Gargoyles in the show, but wouldnt be easier to just make it a variant of Troll? Like the River Hags are (or were, I think C20 they are just a regular kith) for the Redcaps.<br /> <br /> I mean, all changes how need be made are:<br /> - Consider that all of them have an automatic Oath to protect something, so Titan's Power is already in effect.<br /> - Change the Birthright of _Strong of Will and Body_ to _Strength of Stone_ so they also gain two dices of absorptions and they all gain the Merit: Wings.<br /> - Change the Frailty to _Flesh to Stone_ where they became stone on every sunrise and became stone every sundown. As long as they became stone on a place they can use to guard whatever they have the oath to protect (like connected to the building they must protect, or on the house where lives the one they must protect) they are considered in a pacific resting (so recover willpower). If the whatever they should protect ins endangered by whatever reason while on the day, they automatically untransform to protect them, and return to their stone-self when the danger is over. If they fail to protect, or the whatever is seriously harmed, they make a banality trigger.<br /> <br /> It is a rough draft, but I dont think much more is needed. If you want to make they less magic, just add a &quot;to became more resistant to magic, this kith put himself away from it. Their bonuses from Strong of Stone is valid to any magical effect, but also every cantrip they do need an extra success to work&quot;. Should make players less inclined to make magic.<br /> <br /> Also a variant of Golem from the Inanimae could work too. Or a interesting Dark-kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T08:11:53-07:00","id":1209633,"title":"","content":"You could have a group of changeling from an old motley or a specific area all with the advantage Winged &amp; the flaw Cursed (at 5pt) to turn into stone at Dawn.<br /> <br /> That way you could have quite different Gargoyles depending on their initial Kith (and using more merits/flaws you can make them even more apart from other changelings)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T02:56:05-07:00","id":1229331,"title":"","content":"Hmm after reading C20 all the way and reading the Inanimae Secret Ways halfwaythrough I am thinking maybe the first Gargoyles existed after the Sundering but before the Shattering. Maybe the strife of the making war caused some of the Inanimae Krofted, Particularly Mannikins, choose to not be involved in the war. Maybe they use the primordial version of the Changeling Way Ritual/Husk Riding to create Eggs to be reborn in. They were few in Number and spread around the world at different times. But after the crushing of the Empire of Flame and the Shattering and the closing of the Trods a contingent of Inanimae choose to be reborn as Gargoyles rather then Somnulence, noting perhaps their anchors were doomed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or perhaps those Krofted into statues discovered a method of turning their Anchors into Husks to become the first Gargoyles?<br /> <br /> Depending on how we handle Splinters, they need a lot of work, I think maybe one of the options I will use may be allowing Gargoyles to learn one type of Sliver, applying it to Kithain Realms rather than the Inanimae Realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T06:17:59-07:00","id":1229351,"title":"","content":"Maybe [REDACTED] have been around longer than changelings realized, and they only took notice recently.<br /> <br /> \ud83d\ude09\ud83d\ude01","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T20:45:59-07:00","id":1229503,"title":"","content":"Mannikins! I\u2019m guessing Mannikins!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T06:20:12-07:00","id":1387468,"title":"","content":"So it was the Lycians by the way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Returning to this idea since I am working on patching and expanding Slivers. I'm thinking part of the Gargoyle Package is each Gargoyle can learn on Sliver. Or maybe going with my sliver approach defining Slivers as Slivers of Vulgar Phenomena and Slivers of Subtle Phenomena, and Slivers of the Heart Question. And maybe the Siochain/Heart Question state for Gargoyles is becoming Human During the Day rather then slumbering. Therefore maybe I will have it they can choose one Vulgar Sliver, like Stratus to represent their joy in flying paired to Aionios to represent their view on time since they experience time pass twice as fast since they are suspended during the day. Hmm.<br /> <br /> So character Creation would be Choosing a House and building a form as part of their birthright, something like the Mokole dream a form system combined with the Dragonkin system. Hmm if I give them revelries they might have that divided by house. And Houses may have a Favored Art and Element to differentiate them from Changelings who have favored Realms.<br /> <br /> Maybe part of the creation of the Gargoyles involved Inanimae of one Element being tied to a different Element and then miracle into a creature of Flesh by some sort of blessing of Luna or the Night itself. Once again we need a Chthonic Art for the Earth and a Night/Darkness art. Though I have ideas for a Night Dominion which would be something like an Archart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T06:49:52-07:00","id":1387474,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking also of House Pumayyaton/Cythera to represent those who take the form of sculptures of longing and inspiration. They would be the Gargoyle House with a less strict sense of duty, maybe being the mast of a ship, or a sculpture on display, they would also be the Gargoyles with the most human seeming Visage. One of the philosophical questions among the gargoyles could be their attitude and towards duty and freedom being balanced. Are they drawn towards freedom or is freedom just a consequence of their ease in blending with humanity. I can see them being the pariahs of the Gargoyles due to a combination of Jealousy and Disdain. They also would naturally serve a role as ambassadors towards, the Fae, Mannikins, the Prodigals and Humanity as a whole.<br /> <br /> If I do tie it to an element so many work, Stone is an Obvious choice but so is Air that was the breath of life for Galatea and the element the Ship Maidens calm. But Water could also work as Pygmalion was on an Island and Ship Figureheads ride the surf. Or Wood as Cythera's iconic flowers, and the connection to wooden figureheads, and the generative themes Verdage and of the Wood Sliver I am making Ktisis. <br /> <br /> Musing on the Houses they serve a combination of type of Icon as well as their role. But maybe they can have another type like Duty, so you can have an X and Y axis. This way you can have complimentary House and Duty/Archetype, or seemingly weird House and duty mix, like Fenrir Ahroun being complimentary and archetypical, and something like Child of Gaia Ahroun being the at odds nature.<br /> <br /> Still thinking, so many ideas and revisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T09:42:07-07:00","id":1387746,"title":"","content":"I almost feel like a Gargoyle would be a variant of Troll or Ogre with Stone Skin and Wings. I guess I am more used to the &quot;core kith&quot; having subvariance and tweaks, and Gargoyles have always been a form of grotesque meant to ward off evil spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T10:27:05-07:00","id":1387758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicJuggler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1207483-lets-discuss-making-a-gargoyle-kith?p=1387746#post1387746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I almost feel like a Gargoyle would be a variant of Troll or Ogre with Stone Skin and Wings. I guess I am more used to the &quot;core kith&quot; having subvariance and tweaks, and Gargoyles have always been a form of grotesque meant to ward off evil spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah in the olden days that was one of the arguments on how to make gargoyles, along with the trend of making other subkiths like Oni Trolls, and Domovoi Boggans.<br /> <br /> But with the new Changeling Renaissance there has been a bigger push to experiment or go all in.<br /> <br /> And I'm exploring the different types of Gargoyle like statuary with the Houses/Clans, and one of Babewyn's epithets are Grotesques.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T02:10:21-07:00","id":1392453,"title":"","content":"So I am still figuring how I will handle Gargoyles and Arts/Realms/Slivers. I am thinking I will allow them to have access to a Subtle Phenomena Class Sliver and a Vulgar Phenomena Sliver, and probably their own reskin of Realms. I am not sure if I will give them full access to Arts however. Maybe I will allow them to learn a Seasonal Art and Another Art, this will represent they have limited magical potential but a wide array of options, but this is balanced a bit by them having more robust Birthrights, however it is also complicated a bit more by them having potent Frailties, like turning to Stone by Day and a House Fraility/Ban. Or maybe I will just let them be able to just learn Arts like normal, or learn them only up to level 4.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking on how I what form of Realms I will have them use, either Changeling, whatever I come up with for Inanimae or something Unique for Gargoyles like maybe based on Iconography/Guardianship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}